# Build context for frontend/Dockerfile (compose builds with context: ./frontend).
#
# This file exists for correctness, not image size. The Dockerfile runs `COPY . .`
# AFTER installing dependencies, so a node_modules directory riding in from the
# host lands ON TOP of the tree the install just produced — silently replacing
# the lockfile-pinned tree with whatever the developer happens to have, and
# reducing `npm ci` to decoration. This was observed for real while building the
# image locally during ADIM 32. The .dockerignore is what keeps the lockfile
# authoritative; without it the `npm ci` above is not enforceable.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build outputs. dist/ is regenerated by `npm run build` inside the image, so a
# host copy is at best overwritten and at worst a stale bundle shadowing the
# fresh one for any file the build no longer emits.
dist
coverage

# e2e/ is a standalone Playwright package with its own package.json and its own
# lockfile; `npm run build` never reads it (tsconfig.json includes only "src",
# and vite.config.ts excludes "e2e/**" from test discovery). Excluding it
# wholesale covers e2e/node_modules, e2e/test-results and e2e/a11y-report — the
# three named in the RC report — plus 142 tracked screenshot baselines that were
# being shipped into the build context on every build.
e2e

# Local env files never belong in an image layer. Vite gives an already-set
# process env var precedence over .env files, so these could not have altered
# the bundle the Dockerfile's ARG pins — but they can carry a developer's local
# secrets into the context, and .env.example has no use inside the image.
.env
.env.*

# The v18 mockup is a gitignored dev-only copy (CLAUDE.md: `cp docs/spec/...
# frontend/public/mockup_v18.html`). Vite copies public/ verbatim into dist/, so
# without this line a developer who has run that command ships the spec mockup
# into the production image, served by nginx at /mockup_v18.html.
public/mockup_v18.html

# Not inputs to the build.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
.DS_Store
*.log
